; The six face buttons are VRButtons, not plain meshes. One VR hand carries five
; usable inputs and this remote has seven buttons plus a d-pad, so the hand
; binding alone can never reach all of them — 1, 2 and - had nothing to sit on.
; Making the shell itself pokeable closes that the way the hardware does: hold
; the remote in one hand, press the awkward ones with the other. PokeTip gates on
; a hand that is NOT holding something, so a remote can never press its own
; buttons with the hand carrying it.
;
; They press DOWN into the top face (-Y), and each is its own Area3D with the cap
; as its ButtonMesh child so VRButton drives the depress animation itself.
[node name="AButton" type="Area3D" parent="."]
transform = Transform3D(1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0.0155, -0.018)
collision_layer = 0
collision_mask = 0
script = ExtResource("7_vrbtn")
trigger_radius = 0.011
depress_depth = 0.0012
contact_margin = 0.006

